{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "העליתנו", :translit "he'elitanu", :gloss "you brought us up"} {:he "חסר וי\"ו", :translit "chaser vav", :gloss "defective [of] vav"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Spelling anomaly: העליתנו written without a vav, signaling that the complaint targets Moses specifically."}], :frame {:text "The people's complaint in Numbers 20:5 is directed against Moses' leadership. By writing העליתנו defectively (without the expected vav), the verse subtly encodes that the grievance falls specifically on Moses. This is an example of the principle that defective or plene spellings carry exegetical significance.", :sources ["Numbers 20:5"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ותאנה וגפן", :translit "u-te'enah va-gafen", :gloss "and fig and vine"} {:he "ורמון", :translit "ve-rimmon", :gloss "and pomegranate"} {:he "ארץ חטה ושעורה וגפן ותאנה ורמון", :translit "eretz chitah u-se'orah va-gafen u-te'enah va-rimmon", :gloss "land of wheat and barley and vine and fig and pomegranate"} {:he "איש תחת גפנו ותחת תאנתו", :translit "ish tachat gefno ve-tachat te'enato", :gloss "each man under his vine and under his fig tree"} {:he "דסליק מפרה", :translit "de-salik mafreh", :gloss "that ascends from producing fruit"} {:he "בררו משם עצי תאנה", :translit "beraru misham atzei te'enah", :gloss "select from there fig-wood"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ארץ חטה ושעורה וגפן ותאנה ורמון" "ותאנה וגפן ורמון"]} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["איש תחת גפנו ותחת תאנתו" "ותאנה וגפן ורמון"]} {:kind :other, :note "Order reversal: תאנה precedes גפן here (unlike parallel lists) because the fig tree's prominence connects to the command to select fig-wood."}], :frame {:text "Scripture consistently lists the vine (גפן) before the fig (תאנה), as in Deuteronomy 8:8 ('ארץ חטה ושעורה וגפן ותאנה ורמון') and 1 Kings 5:5 ('איש תחת גפנו ותחת תאנתו'). In Numbers 20:5 the order is reversed, with תאנה first. Ba'al HaTurim connects this to Numbers 13:23,